[[File:Auto Retaliate.png|left]]

'''Auto Retaliate''' is a [[Combat]] toggle that allows the player to choose whether their character fights back when attacked. Players can turn it on or off by going to the [[Combat Options]] tab and clicking the icon that says ''"Auto Retaliate (On)/(Off)"''.

The player will attempt to automatically retaliate to the attacker 1 tick after they are attacked for 20 minutes if no player input is given, after which players stop attacking all together even if they are attacked by [[Monster|monsters]]. When a player is attacked, their attack delay is set to their current weapon's attack speed divided by two, rounded up, regardless of what it was prior. 

Turning this option '''off''' is helpful if the player wants to run through an area with lots of [[monsters]] that have [[aggressiveness]], run away from attacking players, or just not fight back when attacked.

It is also recommended to turn Auto Retaliate '''off''' when players are in an area with traps (such as those found in pyramids and dungeons).

Turning Auto Retaliate '''off''' is essential for the prevention of accumulation of combat experience on a [[Skill pure]] build account. 
{| class="wikitable"
|-
| [[File:Auto Retaliate (On).png]] || When Auto Retaliate is '''ON''', the player's character walks/runs towards the monster (or player) attacking and fights back.
|-
| [[File:Auto Retaliate (Off).png]] || When Auto Retaliate is '''OFF''', the player's character just stands where they are and takes the hits from the monster, or another player.
|}

